      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and many guidelines use 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould one of these be what you meant?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for IR.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily**, or a lower starting dose, if the patient is metformin-naive. The usual start is 500 mg once or twice daily, titrated up.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses, if the \"three times daily\" was the error.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified."
      }
     ],
